1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,252
Okay, this one's rare.

2
00:00:02,294 --> 00:00:03,295
This one is medium well.

3
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:04,296
Now go, go, go!

4
00:00:04,338 --> 00:00:05,172
Hey, Phoebe!
Hey!

5
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:05,840
Hey, how was dinner?!

6
00:00:05,881 --> 00:00:07,007
Dinner was good!

7
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:08,509
Just saying hi!
Now I'm going to go!

8
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:12,387
Oh. Well, hello there.

9
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:13,639
Hi.

10
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:15,683
I didn't see this
on the menu.

11
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:16,934
Oh, uh, Tim

12
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:18,268
this is Phoebe,
Phoebe, this is Tim

13
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:19,269
my new sous-chef.

14
00:00:19,311 --> 00:00:21,146
Oh, so your Monica's boss?

15
00:00:21,188 --> 00:00:22,523
Actually, she's my boss.

16
00:00:22,564 --> 00:00:24,191
"Sous" is French for "under."

17
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:26,485
Ah! I sous-stand.

18
00:00:27,026 --> 00:00:28,320
Hey, Tim.

19
00:00:28,362 --> 00:00:29,655
I need a calamari
and a Caesar salad

20
00:00:29,697 --> 00:00:31,031
and could you
give me the pesto?

21
00:00:31,072 --> 00:00:32,031
Yeah.

22
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:33,158
You-you made pesto?

23
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,576
Yes, I did.

24
00:00:34,618 --> 00:00:37,872
Would you say your pesto
is the best-o?

25
00:00:37,913 --> 00:00:40,582
I don't know, but I would
say it's pretty good-o.

26
00:00:40,624 --> 00:00:42,459
( laughing )

27
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:46,045
All right, I still need the
calamari and the Caesar salad.

28
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:47,381
I like your necklace.

29
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,924
Oh, I made it myself.

30
00:00:48,966 --> 00:00:50,384
You are so talented.

31
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:51,927
Well, it's no pesto.

32
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,597
All right, all right, let's just
cut to the chase, okay?

33
00:00:55,639 --> 00:00:56,932
You're single, you're single.

34
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:58,308
He gets off work at 11:00.

35
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:00,019
She'll be waiting
for your call.

36
00:01:00,059 --> 00:01:01,562
I'll give him your number

37
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:04,105
if I could just get one
calamari and one Caesar salad!

38
00:01:06,692 --> 00:01:07,985
I did not yell.

39
00:01:08,027 --> 00:01:09,987
I am not putting
a dollar in the jar.

40
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:22,041
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

41
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,501
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

42
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:27,713
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

43
00:01:27,755 --> 00:01:31,592
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

44
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:35,054
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

45
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:37,222
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

46
00:01:37,264 --> 00:01:40,434
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

47
00:01:40,475 --> 00:01:45,480
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

48
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:53,655
Wow, Bing.

49
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:55,074
Burning the midnight oil.

50
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:56,825
You know me, sir.

51
00:01:56,867 --> 00:01:59,536
Oh, uh, I do have
a question for you.

52
00:01:59,578 --> 00:02:02,372
Do you know how I can get around
the office computer network

53
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:04,541
so I can access
the really good Internet porn?

54
00:02:04,583 --> 00:02:05,834
( laughing )

55
00:02:05,876 --> 00:02:08,003
You're a joker, Bing.

56
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:11,423
What's funny about that?

57
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:13,592
Hey, sorry I kept
you waiting so long.

58
00:02:13,634 --> 00:02:14,760
Hey, that's okay.

59
00:02:14,802 --> 00:02:16,428
So, where do you want to go?

60
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:19,180
Oh, uh, I think you know
where I want to go.

61
00:02:19,222 --> 00:02:20,181
The Hard Rock Cafe?

62
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,934
Yeah.

63
00:02:21,976 --> 00:02:22,810
Again?

64
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:23,852
Yeah!

65
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:27,731
I'm telling you,
I like the food.

66
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:30,358
You like
the Purple Rain display.

67
00:02:31,777 --> 00:02:32,778
Hey, Bob.

68
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:35,363
Hey, Toby, have
a good night.

69
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,658
Did that guy just call you Toby?

70
00:02:38,993 --> 00:02:41,286
Yeah, he thinks
that's my name.

71
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:43,497
Well, why don't
you correct him?

72
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:45,624
Oh, it's been going
on way too long now.

73
00:02:45,666 --> 00:02:47,334
I mean, the first
time he said it

74
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:49,461
we were just passing each
other in the hallway

75
00:02:49,503 --> 00:02:50,796
so I didn't say anything

76
00:02:50,838 --> 00:02:52,422
and then the
next time he said

77
00:02:52,464 --> 00:02:54,133
"Hey, Toby, you
want a doughnut?"

78
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:55,676
and, I-I wanted
a doughnut.

79
00:02:56,969 --> 00:02:58,720
And now it's
five years later

80
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:01,098
the doughnut's gone
and I'm still Toby.

81
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:03,517
Five years? Chandler,
you have to tell him.

82
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:05,019
No, that would be so awkward.

83
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:07,479
Look, besides, we work in
different departments.

84
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:09,230
He's on the sixth
floor, you know.

85
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:11,066
So he calls me Toby
once in a while.

86
00:03:11,108 --> 00:03:12,109
What's the big deal?

87
00:03:12,151 --> 00:03:13,276
Could be worse.

88
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:14,862
It's not like he's
calling me Muriel.

89
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,195
Muriel.

90
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:18,032
Why would he
call you Muriel?

91
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:24,663
Oh, my God.

92
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:29,084
Chandler M. Bing.

93
00:03:31,086 --> 00:03:32,379
It's not just an "M."

94
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,840
Your middle name is Muriel!

95
00:03:34,882 --> 00:03:36,050
Shh!

96
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:38,135
It is a family name.

97
00:03:38,177 --> 00:03:42,514
Chandler Muriel Bing.

98
00:03:42,556 --> 00:03:45,642
Boy, your parents never even
gave you a chance, did they?

99
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:50,397
Drake, I've discovered
the reason for all

100
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:51,982
your headaches
and memory loss.

101
00:03:52,024 --> 00:03:53,650
What is it?

102
00:03:53,692 --> 00:03:56,737
Apparently your brain transplant
was not entirely successful.

103
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:59,489
It seems your body
is rejecting Jessica's brain.

104
00:03:59,531 --> 00:04:01,909
Is it serious?

105
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,494
Not if we extract tissue
from the original host body

106
00:04:04,536 --> 00:04:07,455
synthesize antibodies, and
introduce them into your system

107
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:10,458
which could stop it
from rejecting the brain.

108
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,293
Well, that sounds
simple enough.

109
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:13,461
Let's just do that.

110
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:14,755
We would

111
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:18,133
but when we went to
exhume Jessica's body

112
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:19,593
it was gone.

113
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:27,059
DIRECTOR:
Cut! Very nice, people.

114
00:04:27,101 --> 00:04:28,435
Okay, let me just get changed,
then we can go to dinner.

115
00:04:28,476 --> 00:04:30,562
Well, what happened
to Jessica's body?

116
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:32,647
I'm not telling.
You'll have to see it on TV.

117
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:35,234
You don't know, do you?

118
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:37,152
No. Couldn't care less.

119
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:38,277
Hey, good scene, man.

120
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:39,279
Hey, you, too.

121
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,280
All right.

122
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:43,617
( clearing throat )

123
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:44,993
What? You weren't in it.

124
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:46,036
Oh!

125
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:48,830
Oh, sorry.

126
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:50,331
Uh, Cash,
this is my friend Rachel.

127
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:51,917
Rachel, Cash.
Cash, Rachel.

128
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:53,418
Hi.
Hi.

129
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,045
So how come I haven't
seen you here before?

130
00:04:55,087 --> 00:04:58,465
Well, Joey probably just
thinks I'll embarrass him.

131
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:01,468
He thinks I'm some kind
of a soap opera nut.

132
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:02,928
Which I'm not, I'm not.

133
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:04,138
( laughing )

134
00:05:04,179 --> 00:05:05,597
Although, I do know

135
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:08,976
that your favorite ice cream
flavor is butter pecan

136
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:13,730
and, uh, and that
your dog's name is Wally.

137
00:05:13,772 --> 00:05:16,942
Well, look at that,
I'm just stroking your arm.

138
00:05:16,984 --> 00:05:17,985
Here we go! Here we go.

139
00:05:18,026 --> 00:05:18,986
Oh, we're leaving.

140
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:19,987
Bye, Cash.
Bye.

141
00:05:20,028 --> 00:05:21,029
Say hi to Wally.

142
00:05:26,118 --> 00:05:27,161
Ooh, Monica.

143
00:05:27,202 --> 00:05:28,203
Hi.

144
00:05:28,245 --> 00:05:29,454
Oh, my God.

145
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:32,082
I had the best time
with Tim last night.

146
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:33,416
He is so sweet.

147
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:36,170
Oh, I can't wait to
get sous-neath him.

148
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:37,420
Uh...

149
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:39,173
I, I have to fire him.

150
00:05:39,214 --> 00:05:40,507
But why?

151
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:42,050
Because he's
terrible. Okay?

152
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:43,844
He's slow,
he burns things.

153
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:46,680
Last night he lit
my pastry chef on fire.

154
00:05:46,721 --> 00:05:47,973
Maybe he was just nervous.

155
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:49,891
You know, you can be
very intimidating.

156
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:51,810
Besides, I've
met your pastry chef

157
00:05:51,852 --> 00:05:54,188
and she can stand to be
taken down a peg or two.

158
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:55,647
Well, now she
has no eyebrows.

159
00:05:55,689 --> 00:05:56,690
Mission accomplished.

160
00:05:57,816 --> 00:06:01,611
But Monica,
he loves his job so much.

161
00:06:01,653 --> 00:06:04,823
Can't you just give him
another chance, please?

162
00:06:06,825 --> 00:06:09,119
All right, but if he lights
someone else on fire

163
00:06:09,161 --> 00:06:10,120
he is out of there!

164
00:06:10,162 --> 00:06:11,579
That's fair.

165
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:14,791
Thank you so much. Thanks.

166
00:06:14,833 --> 00:06:16,668
Oops. Looks like when
he got the pastry chef

167
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:17,961
he got you a little bit, too.

168
00:06:18,003 --> 00:06:21,256
I paid to have this done.

169
00:06:23,175 --> 00:06:24,592
Love it!

170
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:29,597
Hey.
Hi.

171
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:32,642
Oh, you know, Cash really
liked you the other day.

172
00:06:32,684 --> 00:06:34,269
He said he thought
you were charming.

173
00:06:34,311 --> 00:06:36,897
Oh, I thought
I was a complete idiot.

174
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,565
Hey, I'm with you.

175
00:06:38,606 --> 00:06:40,150
He even asked me

176
00:06:40,192 --> 00:06:42,152
if I thought you'd
go out with him.

177
00:06:42,194 --> 00:06:45,613
Oh, Oh, I think I'm going
to throw up a little bit.

178
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:46,740
What did you say?

179
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:47,741
I said no.

180
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:48,909
What?!

181
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:51,912
I just figured
since you're pregnant

182
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:54,373
you're not going
to be seeing people.

183
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:56,415
Okay, Joey...

184
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:57,667
First of all

185
00:06:57,709 --> 00:07:00,087
Cash Ford-- not people.

186
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,963
Second of all,
what did he say

187
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:03,965
when you told him
I was pregnant?

188
00:07:04,007 --> 00:07:05,217
I didn't tell him.

189
00:07:05,259 --> 00:07:07,135
I didn't know if you
were telling people.

190
00:07:07,177 --> 00:07:09,971
This is back when I thought
Cash was still people.

191
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:10,972
Okay, don't tell him,

192
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:12,182
Just have him
call me, okay?

193
00:07:12,224 --> 00:07:13,934
I really don't think
that's a great...

194
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:15,435
Okay, You go do it!
I'll come back

195
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:17,271
and meet more actors.
I'll meet them all!

196
00:07:17,312 --> 00:07:18,313
Yup.

197
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:21,942
Hey, Bob.

198
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:24,361
Hey, how's my pal Toby
doing today?

199
00:07:24,403 --> 00:07:25,862
If I see him, I'll ask.

200
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:26,863
Toby!

201
00:07:26,905 --> 00:07:27,906
No, no, no, no, no.

202
00:07:30,117 --> 00:07:31,743
Hey, hey, Bing.

203
00:07:31,785 --> 00:07:34,079
Was that Bob from Six
you were just talking to?

204
00:07:34,121 --> 00:07:35,163
Yeah, that was him.

205
00:07:35,205 --> 00:07:36,915
Well, then you
know each other.

206
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:38,750
We're on a semi
first-name basis.

207
00:07:38,792 --> 00:07:41,420
What do you think of
adding him to our team?

208
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:42,421
Bob?

209
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:44,756
Ooh. Working here with us?

210
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:46,049
Every day?

211
00:07:46,091 --> 00:07:48,969
Yeah, I don't know
if he has what it takes.

212
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:49,970
Really?

213
00:07:50,011 --> 00:07:51,388
They love him down on Six.

214
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:53,932
But this is 11.

215
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:57,352
It's almost twice
as hard up here.

216
00:07:57,394 --> 00:07:59,104
Okay, I hear you
loud and clear.

217
00:07:59,146 --> 00:08:00,188
Bob will stay put.

218
00:08:00,230 --> 00:08:01,564
I think it's best, sir.

219
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:03,483
But we really do need to
find someone up here.

220
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:05,026
The work is starting
to pile up.

221
00:08:05,068 --> 00:08:07,446
I've got a stack of documents
on my desk this high.

222
00:08:07,486 --> 00:08:09,197
You know what
you should do?

223
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:12,826
Just toss them in the shredder
and claim you never got them.

224
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:13,952
( laughing )

225
00:08:13,994 --> 00:08:16,621
That's a good one, Bing.

226
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:18,123
What does a guy have to do

227
00:08:18,165 --> 00:08:20,167
to be taken seriously
around here?

228
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:26,298
Hey.
Hey.

229
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:27,799
Okay, I gave him
another chance

230
00:08:27,841 --> 00:08:28,967
but Tim has got to go.

231
00:08:29,009 --> 00:08:30,260
But...
No. No, no.

232
00:08:30,302 --> 00:08:31,886
He is totally incompetent.

233
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:34,973
Okay, I called the chef who
recommended him to me.

234
00:08:35,015 --> 00:08:36,641
He said, "Ha, ha! Gotcha!"

235
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:39,478
Okay, okay, but
you can't fire him today.

236
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:40,520
Why not?

237
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:42,022
Because I'm
dumping him today.

238
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:43,648
What? You said he was so sweet.

239
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:44,649
He is sweet.

240
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:45,984
He's too sweet!

241
00:08:46,026 --> 00:08:47,610
He calls me all the time.

242
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:50,113
"So, did you get home
from work okay?"

243
00:08:50,155 --> 00:08:52,491
"Did you get out
of the shower okay?"

244
00:08:52,531 --> 00:08:54,117
Well, just don't
pick up your phone.

245
00:08:54,159 --> 00:08:55,243
Then he comes over.

246
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:56,870
"I'm so worried about you."

247
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:58,038
Ugh, be a man!

248
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,624
What? So now I'm
not allowed to fire him?

249
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:04,044
We can't fire him
and dump him in the same day.

250
00:09:04,085 --> 00:09:05,170
He'll kill himself.

251
00:09:05,212 --> 00:09:06,671
I'll fire him today
and you go out

252
00:09:06,713 --> 00:09:07,714
with him for another week.

253
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:09,257
Are you kidding?

254
00:09:09,299 --> 00:09:11,843
Another week with that simp,
I'll kill myself.

255
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:13,594
Okay, well, then
we'll both do it today

256
00:09:13,636 --> 00:09:15,305
and he'll just have
to deal with it.

257
00:09:15,347 --> 00:09:18,058
Okay, but the question is,
who's going to go first?

258
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:20,935
'Cause whoever goes second
is the bitch.

259
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:22,020
What do you mean?

260
00:09:22,062 --> 00:09:23,021
Come on.

261
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:24,398
The boss that fires a guy

262
00:09:24,439 --> 00:09:26,149
that's just been dumped? Bitch!

263
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:29,069
And the woman who dumps a guy
that's just been fired?

264
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:31,154
Blonde bitch!

265
00:09:31,196 --> 00:09:32,531
I wanted to do this days ago

266
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:35,409
so I think I should go first.

267
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:36,701
Ugh, that makes sense.

268
00:09:36,743 --> 00:09:38,370
Errgh, but...

269
00:09:38,412 --> 00:09:41,581
Screw you, I'm going first!

270
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,255
Hey, Toby, you got a sec?

271
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,256
Sure, what's up?

272
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,673
I just had a meeting.

273
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:52,842
I was actually hoping
to get transferred up here

274
00:09:52,884 --> 00:09:55,011
but I just found out
it's not going to happen.

275
00:09:55,053 --> 00:09:57,680
Apparently somebody thinks
I'm not 11th floor material.

276
00:09:57,722 --> 00:09:59,391
Say, uh...

277
00:09:59,433 --> 00:10:02,685
Who the hell
is this Chandler?

278
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:07,399
Hey, what do you think
is a better excuse

279
00:10:07,441 --> 00:10:09,817
for why I'm not drinking
on this date tonight--

280
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:11,236
I'm a recovering alcoholic

281
00:10:11,278 --> 00:10:12,946
I'm a Mormon

282
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:16,575
or I got so hammered last night,
I'm still a little drunk?

283
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:17,576
Hey.

284
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:18,785
Hi.
Hey.

285
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:21,538
So, what do you
want to do tonight?

286
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:23,457
There's a Ukrainian
film at the Angelica

287
00:10:23,498 --> 00:10:25,833
that's supposed to be very
powerful. Interested?

288
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:29,421
No. No, but I'll go see
a normal-person movie with you.

289
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:31,590
Rach, you want to come?

290
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:33,383
Oh, no, I can't. I got a date.

291
00:10:33,425 --> 00:10:36,177
A date?

292
00:10:36,219 --> 00:10:38,637
Yeah. Why, is that
weird for you?

293
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:41,391
Why, no, it's
the opposite of weird.

294
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:43,310
It's, it's, uh, regular.

295
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:45,353
It's, it's uh... mundane.

296
00:10:45,395 --> 00:10:48,022
It's, it's actually
a little dull.

297
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:50,191
It's no Ukrainian film,
I tell you.

298
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:52,319
Ooh, earrings!

299
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:55,363
A date?

300
00:10:55,405 --> 00:10:58,074
She's got a date? With who?

301
00:10:58,116 --> 00:10:59,993
I set her up
with this actor on my show.

302
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:01,453
You set her up?

303
00:11:01,495 --> 00:11:04,914
No.

304
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:06,458
Joey, what were you thinking?

305
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,251
I was thinking that
it'd probably be okay

306
00:11:08,293 --> 00:11:10,711
because Ross hasn't gone out
with Rachel in five years.

307
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:12,797
Joey, I'm not
worried about her.

308
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:14,591
I'm worried about my baby.

309
00:11:14,633 --> 00:11:16,759
Whoever she dates,
my baby dates.

310
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:19,678
Now, now, where is this
"actor" taking them?

311
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:22,098
Hey! I'm an "actor" too.

312
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:26,394
I'm not sure. I think
they're taking the ferry

313
00:11:26,436 --> 00:11:28,438
out to some Italian place
on Staten Island.

314
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:31,232
A ferry?
My baby is going on a ferry.

315
00:11:31,274 --> 00:11:34,819
Do you have any idea how
dangerous those are?!

316
00:11:34,861 --> 00:11:37,572
Aren't we talking about those
big boats that carry cars?

317
00:11:37,614 --> 00:11:39,157
They go like
five miles an hour?

318
00:11:39,199 --> 00:11:41,535
Why don't they just jump
out of an airplane, huh?

319
00:11:41,576 --> 00:11:42,619
That's a fun date.

320
00:11:42,661 --> 00:11:44,204
Or burn each other with matches.

321
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:45,288
That's fun, too. Woo!

322
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:47,081
( knocking )

323
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:50,210
Hey, Joey.

324
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:51,670
Hey, Cash.
Uh, hey, this is Ross.

325
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:52,671
Ross, this is Cash.

326
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:53,921
Hey.
Hey.

327
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:55,965
I hear you're going
on a ferry tonight.

328
00:11:56,007 --> 00:11:57,091
Yeah.
Yeah.

329
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:59,135
Bit of a daredevil, are we?

330
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:01,846
Hey, you guys.

331
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:03,764
Do you think this
is too slutty? Hi, Cash.

332
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:05,099
Hey, Rachel.
Hi.

333
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,518
Ready to go?

334
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,019
Yeah. All right,
I'll see you guys later.

335
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:10,313
Okay. Have
a great time, you guys.

336
00:12:10,355 --> 00:12:11,314
Thank you.
Thank you.

337
00:12:11,356 --> 00:12:12,399
Yes, it is too slutty!

338
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:21,949
Hi.

339
00:12:21,991 --> 00:12:23,284
( gasps )

340
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:24,661
Hi.

341
00:12:24,703 --> 00:12:26,079
I'm so glad you called.

342
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,664
I feel like it's always
me calling you.

343
00:12:27,706 --> 00:12:29,999
So, what's up?

344
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:32,168
Is everything okay
with Phoebe?

345
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:35,171
It will be, in a minute.

346
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:39,092
Listen-- Tim, you're
a really great guy.

347
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:40,552
That's because
I'm with you.

348
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:41,886
Aww.

349
00:12:44,556 --> 00:12:48,351
I'm just, I'm in a place
in my life right now where I...

350
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:49,519
( loud beeping )

351
00:12:49,561 --> 00:12:51,271
Oops. I'm so sorry.

352
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:52,439
This just in.

353
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,772
( laughing )

354
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:55,567
Oh, it's 911
from the restaurant.

355
00:12:55,609 --> 00:12:57,611
That means Monica
needs me right away.

356
00:12:57,652 --> 00:12:58,737
Oh, oh, no, she doesn't!

357
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:00,405
I know what that is;
you can stay.

358
00:13:00,447 --> 00:13:03,658
Aww. I'll miss you,
too, Pheebs.

359
00:13:04,743 --> 00:13:06,827
And I will be
holding you...

360
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:08,871
right here.

361
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:18,923
So, what movie
do you want to see?

362
00:13:18,965 --> 00:13:21,092
And not another one
I have to read, okay?

363
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,801
I get enough of
that from books.

364
00:13:24,262 --> 00:13:25,680
Books?

365
00:13:25,722 --> 00:13:28,224
All right, car magazines,
cereal boxes...

366
00:13:28,266 --> 00:13:29,892
but it's, like, enough!

367
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:32,061
Well, I'll tell you what,
why don't we, uh...

368
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:33,438
why don't we just stay here?

369
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,315
Let's not see a movie;
we'll just hang.

370
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:37,858
And just wait for Rachel
to come back from her date?

371
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:41,070
Hey, if that's what you want
to do, I'm not going to say no.

372
00:13:41,112 --> 00:13:45,158
Dude, what is going on?

373
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:47,118
I just... I have to
find out how it went.

374
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,369
Why?

375
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:50,622
This guy could be
my baby's stepfather.

376
00:13:50,664 --> 00:13:51,998
They go on one date

377
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:53,874
and you're worried about
them getting married?

378
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:54,875
He's not you!

379
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:57,629
I just... I...

380
00:13:57,671 --> 00:13:59,838
I can't believe she's...
she's dating.

381
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,717
Well, Ross, what did you
think she was going to do?

382
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:04,260
I don't know.

383
00:14:04,302 --> 00:14:07,930
I guess I just can't believe
any of this is happening.

384
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:09,848
Wh-What do you mean?

385
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:11,225
It's just that I always thought

386
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:13,060
when I had another kid,
it'd be different.

387
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:14,813
You know,
I-I love Ben

388
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:20,109
but every time I have to drop
him off at Carol and Susan's...

389
00:14:20,151 --> 00:14:22,862
it's like, it breaks
my heart a little.

390
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:26,949
I mean, I-I've always had this
picture of me and my next wife

391
00:14:26,991 --> 00:14:28,493
in bed on Sunday

392
00:14:28,535 --> 00:14:31,788
and my kid comes running in
and leaps up onto the bed

393
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:34,749
and we all read the paper
together, you know?

394
00:14:34,791 --> 00:14:38,877
Maybe fight over
the Science Section.

395
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:39,962
That's a nice picture.

396
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:41,589
Maybe you could
still have that.

397
00:14:41,631 --> 00:14:42,799
No, no, I can't.

398
00:14:42,841 --> 00:14:45,468
I mean, Rachel's out
with some guy.

399
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:48,471
My baby went with her.

400
00:14:48,513 --> 00:14:54,143
Well, if anything, that picture
keeps moving further away.

401
00:14:54,185 --> 00:14:56,646
Hey, can I ask you something?

402
00:14:56,688 --> 00:15:00,941
In this... in this picture
of you and your wife...

403
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:03,277
is your wife Rachel?

404
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:06,781
It used to be.

405
00:15:06,823 --> 00:15:11,452
Now-now she doesn't
really have a face.

406
00:15:11,494 --> 00:15:14,664
Smokin' body, though.

407
00:15:14,706 --> 00:15:17,208
Yeah, good call.

408
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:21,337
Yeah, but the face, Ross,
the face isn't Rachel.

409
00:15:21,379 --> 00:15:25,675
No, but... aah, how much easier
would it be if it were.

410
00:15:25,717 --> 00:15:28,010
Yeah, I know, but I don't
think that's what she wants.

411
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:29,763
No, it's not
what I want, either.

412
00:15:29,804 --> 00:15:32,223
I mean, I can't force myself
to fall in love with her again.

413
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:35,476
Okay, Ross, maybe you
need a new picture. Okay?

414
00:15:35,518 --> 00:15:39,439
It's not going to be what you
thought, but no matter what

415
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:42,525
there's going to be
a brand-new little baby.

416
00:15:42,567 --> 00:15:44,193
Your baby.

417
00:15:44,235 --> 00:15:48,114
Who cares what the
picture looks like.

418
00:15:48,155 --> 00:15:50,116
Yeah.

419
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:52,118
Hey, tell
you what.

420
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:54,537
Let's you and me go out
and have some fun, huh?

421
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:55,996
Whatever you want. Come on.

422
00:15:57,916 --> 00:16:00,293
We can still catch
that Ukrainian film.

423
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:02,044
No, I said fun.

424
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:05,339
Hey, Toby.

425
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:06,633
Hey, Bobby.

426
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:08,342
It's "Bob," actually.

427
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:11,137
Hey, you work up here.

428
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:14,056
Can you tell me where this
Chandler Bing's office is?

429
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:16,058
Uh... yeah.

430
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:19,103
Yeah, it's... it's
right-right-right down...

431
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:20,104
Yeah.

432
00:16:20,146 --> 00:16:21,230
Right there.

433
00:16:21,272 --> 00:16:23,190
Yeah. Let me ask you, why?

434
00:16:23,232 --> 00:16:26,193
I want to talk to that bastard,
see what his problem is.

435
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:28,195
Okay, Bob, listen, uh...

436
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:31,783
I'm the reason you didn't
get the job up here.

437
00:16:31,825 --> 00:16:33,910
Toby, don't.

438
00:16:33,952 --> 00:16:35,411
Bob...

439
00:16:35,453 --> 00:16:39,415
Toby, I'm not going to
let you cover for him.

440
00:16:39,457 --> 00:16:40,875
Anything you say right now

441
00:16:40,917 --> 00:16:43,210
will just get me more
upset with Chandler.

442
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:46,881
Well, that puts me
in a difficult position.

443
00:16:48,591 --> 00:16:49,550
Hey.
Hey.

444
00:16:49,592 --> 00:16:50,885
I got your page.

445
00:16:50,927 --> 00:16:52,261
Is everything okay?

446
00:16:52,303 --> 00:16:53,471
Uh, well, th-that depends.

447
00:16:53,513 --> 00:16:54,764
How are things with Phoebe?

448
00:16:54,806 --> 00:16:56,140
Oh, it's great.
It's great.

449
00:16:56,182 --> 00:16:57,851
Thank you so much
for introducing us.

450
00:16:57,892 --> 00:16:59,853
Oh, my pleasure.

451
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:02,313
Okay, I'm afraid
I've got some bad news.

452
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:03,898
Phoebe!

453
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:05,441
Monica!

454
00:17:05,483 --> 00:17:06,734
PHOEBE:
I'm...

455
00:17:06,776 --> 00:17:08,695
I'm breaking
up with you!
You're fired!

456
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:09,737
What?

457
00:17:09,779 --> 00:17:11,906
I'm-I'm breaking up with you.

458
00:17:11,948 --> 00:17:13,616
You're fired.

459
00:17:13,658 --> 00:17:15,326
Wh-Why?

460
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:16,995
I'm sorry, I'm just, I'm...

461
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:19,789
I'm just not ready
for a relationship right now.

462
00:17:19,831 --> 00:17:22,375
An-And I'm sorry, too, but...

463
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:24,878
Well, I just, I like
things done a certain way

464
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:26,796
and the chemistry's
just not right.

465
00:17:26,838 --> 00:17:27,881
Ooh, that's good.

466
00:17:27,922 --> 00:17:29,966
The chemistry thing for us, too.

467
00:17:30,008 --> 00:17:32,760
Wow.

468
00:17:32,802 --> 00:17:34,554
Um, okay.

469
00:17:34,595 --> 00:17:36,305
Um...

470
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:38,432
I-I-I-I realize
I came on a little strong

471
00:17:38,474 --> 00:17:40,977
but it's only because
I think you're so amazing.

472
00:17:41,019 --> 00:17:43,980
And, uh,
I-I just want to...

473
00:17:44,022 --> 00:17:46,524
I want to tell you
how much I appreciate you

474
00:17:46,566 --> 00:17:48,985
giving me an opportunity here
because I...

475
00:17:49,027 --> 00:17:51,821
You're the most talented chef
I ever worked for.

476
00:17:53,364 --> 00:17:55,408
Anyway...

477
00:18:00,663 --> 00:18:01,956
Tim, wait.

478
00:18:01,998 --> 00:18:03,123
Yeah?

479
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:05,084
Um...

480
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:06,836
I think I spoke too quickly.

481
00:18:06,878 --> 00:18:09,839
Th-There's a learning curve
with this job, and...

482
00:18:09,881 --> 00:18:11,674
maybe we could try it again.

483
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:13,217
Really?
Yeah.

484
00:18:13,259 --> 00:18:15,261
Thank you so much, because
I know I can be better.

485
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:16,804
Okay.

486
00:18:16,846 --> 00:18:21,350
And, Tim... I just want
to say good luck here.

487
00:18:29,067 --> 00:18:30,192
Hello.

488
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:31,193
Hi.

489
00:18:31,235 --> 00:18:32,194
( chuckles )

490
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:33,529
How was the date?

491
00:18:33,571 --> 00:18:34,989
Well, I'm alone

492
00:18:35,031 --> 00:18:38,076
and I just bought $15
worth of candy bars.

493
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:39,535
What do you think?

494
00:18:39,577 --> 00:18:40,536
Uh-huh.

495
00:18:40,578 --> 00:18:42,329
What happened?

496
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:45,207
Made the mistake of telling
him that I was pregnant.

497
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:47,877
Oh, he didn't, uh,
take it so well?

498
00:18:47,919 --> 00:18:49,629
Well, better than you.

499
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:52,381
But, you know, still
not what you want.

500
00:18:52,423 --> 00:18:53,716
Oh?

501
00:18:53,758 --> 00:18:55,802
Yeah, he got all
weird and sputtery

502
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:57,553
and then he said, uh

503
00:18:57,595 --> 00:19:00,765
"Yeah, I hear those
hemorrhoids are a bitch."

504
00:19:00,807 --> 00:19:02,266
He sounds swell.

505
00:19:02,308 --> 00:19:03,935
Doesn't he? Mm.

506
00:19:03,977 --> 00:19:06,771
Hey, you want a...
you want a little cheering up?

507
00:19:06,813 --> 00:19:07,772
Yes.

508
00:19:07,814 --> 00:19:08,773
Sit down.

509
00:19:08,815 --> 00:19:10,024
Okay.

510
00:19:10,066 --> 00:19:13,111
Guess whose middle name
is Muriel.

511
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:17,615
( gasps )

512
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:19,075
Chandler M. Bing.

513
00:19:19,117 --> 00:19:19,659
Yeah-uh.

514
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:21,577
Oh, my God.

515
00:19:21,619 --> 00:19:23,704
( chortles )

516
00:19:23,746 --> 00:19:25,539
Hmm...

517
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:27,374
I'm sorry about your date.

518
00:19:27,416 --> 00:19:29,293
Aw, it's all right.

519
00:19:29,335 --> 00:19:32,296
I guess I'm just done with
the whole dating thing.

520
00:19:32,338 --> 00:19:34,590
It's just one more
thing in my life

521
00:19:34,632 --> 00:19:37,093
that is suddenly
completely different.

522
00:19:37,135 --> 00:19:38,845
This is hard.

523
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:41,806
Yeah, I know.

524
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:47,478
On the other hand, in, uh...
in about seven months

525
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:51,065
you're going to have something
that you're going to love

526
00:19:51,107 --> 00:19:54,568
more than any guy
you've ever gone out with.

527
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:57,780
Just wait.

528
00:19:57,822 --> 00:19:59,782
Wait until, uh...

529
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:03,995
Wait until the first time
your baby grabs your finger.

530
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:06,372
You have no idea.

531
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:10,501
Thanks, sweetie.

532
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:12,045
Mm-mm.

533
00:20:14,047 --> 00:20:16,632
You, uh, you want
to grab some coffee?

534
00:20:16,674 --> 00:20:19,844
Oh, no. I think
I'm going to go home
and eat ten candy bars.

535
00:20:19,886 --> 00:20:22,429
Hey, I-I thought
I cheered you up.

536
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:24,348
Oh, you did--
there are 20 in here.

537
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:25,850
Right.

538
00:20:25,892 --> 00:20:26,851
Good night.

539
00:20:26,893 --> 00:20:28,061
Good night.

540
00:20:35,193 --> 00:20:36,485
Ross?

541
00:20:36,527 --> 00:20:37,653
Yeah?

542
00:20:37,695 --> 00:20:38,863
Hey, it's Mona.

543
00:20:38,905 --> 00:20:40,322
From the wedding.

544
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:41,407
Oh, hi!

545
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:42,909
Hi.

546
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:44,994
Wow, uh... how are you?

547
00:20:45,036 --> 00:20:48,330
I'm good, except, um,
you still owe me a dance.

548
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:50,208
Oh, that's
right.
Mm.

549
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:51,959
Well, uh, would you
be interested

550
00:20:52,001 --> 00:20:53,419
in seeing a Ukrainian film?

551
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:55,546
( cracking up )

552
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:57,715
Oh, you're serious. Sure.

553
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:02,261
ROSS:
Great, well, um...

554
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:04,680
I-I think I might need
one more cup of coffee.

555
00:21:04,722 --> 00:21:06,390
Sure. Let me get it for you.

556
00:21:06,432 --> 00:21:07,433
Okay.

557
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:26,786
Bob.

558
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:28,246
Bob!

559
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:29,622
Bob!

560
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:32,208
What the hell are you doing?!

561
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:35,293
I just found out
this is Chandler's office.

562
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:37,755
Come on, Toby, give me a hand.

563
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:44,428
